  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Seasonably cooler this weekend into next week \nwith bulk of precipitation confined near and southeast of Lake \nErie\n\nFollowing one of the warmest starts to November on record in\ncentral PA, (see climate section) we'll make a trip on the\nweather coaster back to seasonably cooler temps this weekend \nthrough the upcoming work week (though a slight rebound in temps\nwill occur Sunday through Tuesday). \n\nA compact and seasonably strong closed upper low near Buffalo,\nNY this afternoon will move across southern New York and lift \nnortheast away from the area by Sunday morning. This feature \naccompanied by cool air aloft and mean west to NW flow will \nbring scattered to numerous showers to start the first full \nweekend of November.\n\nThe rest of today into early next week will be noticeably \ncooler and feel rather chilly given how warm it has been during \nthe day over the past week or so. Breezy conditions will help to\nbring the chill factor. Max Wind gusts will top out in the mid \n25-35mph range and could peak around 40 mph on Monday. \n\nThere is a growing model signal for a more substantial long \nwave trough to carve out over the eastern U.S. by the end of \nthe week. While still very preliminary given the extended\nforecast length and associated uncertainly/low confidence, it\nappears the coldest air of the Fall season will attempt to\nexpand southward late next week with the upper trough and could\nbe a factor with a potential coastal storm supplying a swath of\nprecipitation including accumulating snow particularly in the\nhigher elevations.",
